cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AI Payback Assessment"
message: "If you use this instrument, please cite both the software and the paper it implements."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Yedigeyeva"
    given-names: "Madina"
    alias: "Madina K. Yedigeyeva"
repository-code: "https://github.com/madinaedigeeva/ai-payback"
abstract: >-
  An open instrument for assessing whether an enterprise AI adoption programme
  is positioned to pay back. It scores 60 diagnostic questions across 20
  barriers in three layers weighted after BCG's 10-20-70 allocation, builds a
  total cost of ownership across the categories most often omitted from AI
  budgets, and renders the ROI analysis artifact that AI adoption maturity
  frameworks require but do not define. Every coefficient carries a provenance
  tier; claims that could not be traced to a reachable primary source are
  published as excluded rather than used.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - AI adoption
  - return on investment
  - total cost of ownership
  - technology management
  - assessment instrument
license: Apache-2.0
